00:23:28,680 --> 00:23:33,840
splendid I've never seen you really and absolutely angry, but I can fancy how

266
00:23:33,840 --> 00:23:38,639
delightful you looked. And, after all, you said something to me the day before

267
00:23:38,639 --> 00:23:43,799
yesterday that seemed to me at the time to be merely fanciful, but that I see now

268
00:23:43,799 --> 00:23:51,559
was absolutely true, and it holds the key to everything.” “What was that, Harry?” “You said

269
00:23:51,559 --> 00:23:56,398
to me that cibil van represented to you all the heroins of romance— —that she was

270
00:23:56,398 --> 00:24:02,680
Desdemona one night, and ofilia the other; that if she died as Juliet, she came to

271
00:24:02,680 --> 00:24:07,318
life as imagin She will never come to life again now,”

272
00:24:07,318 --> 00:24:12,000
