273
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:18,799
“No, she will never come to life. She has played her last part. But you must think

274
00:24:18,799 --> 00:24:22,840
of that lonely death in the Torre dressing room simply as a strange lurid

275
00:24:22,840 --> 00:24:29,639
fragment from some jacoban tragedy, as a wonderful scene from Webster, or Ford, or

276
00:24:29,639 --> 00:24:36,439
sirel toer The girl never really lived, and so she has never really died. To you

277
00:24:36,439 --> 00:24:40,199
at least she was always a dream, a phantom that flitted through

278
00:24:40,199 --> 00:24:45,600
Shakespeare’s plays and left them lovelier for its presence, a read through

