00:24:45,600 --> 00:24:50,079
which Shakespeare’s music sounded richer and more full of joy. The moment she

280
00:24:50,079 --> 00:24:56,520
touched actual life, she marred it, and it marred her, and so she passed away. Mourn

281
00:24:56,520 --> 00:25:01,000
for ailia if you like. Put ashes on your head because Cordelia was

282
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:06,478
strangled. Cry out against Heaven because the daughter of Brabantio died. But don’t

283
00:25:06,478 --> 00:25:12,680
waste your tears over Cil vain She was less real than they are.” There was a

284
00:25:12,680 --> 00:25:16,120
silence. The evening darkened in the room.

285
00:25:16,120 --> 00:25:20,719
Noiselessly, and with silver feet, the shadows crept in from the

286
00:25:20,719 --> 00:25:27,439
garden. The colors faded wearily out of things. After some time Dorian Gray looked

287
00:25:27,439 --> 00:25:33,079
up. “You have explained me to myself, Harry,” he murmured with something of a sigh of

288
00:25:33,079 --> 00:25:38,398
relief. “I felt all that you have said, but somehow I was afraid of it, and I could

289
00:25:38,398 --> 00:25:43,318
not express it to myself. How well you know me! But we will

290
00:25:43,318 --> 00:25:49,719
not talk again of what has happened. It has been a marvelous experience. That is

291
00:25:49,719 --> 00:25:55,279
all. I wonder if life has still in store for me anything as marvelous Life has

