00:28:56,920 --> 00:29:01,359
be as a wonderful tragic figure sent onto the world stage to show the supreme

327
00:29:01,359 --> 00:29:07,639
reality of love. A wonderful tragic figure? Tears came to his eyes as he

328
00:29:07,639 --> 00:29:13,840
remembered her childlike look, and winsome fanciful ways, and shy tremulous

329
00:29:13,840 --> 00:29:18,040
grace. He brushed them away hastily and looked again at the

330
00:29:18,040 --> 00:29:22,398
picture. He felt that the time had really come for making his

331
00:29:22,398 --> 00:29:29,719
choice. Or had his choice already been made? Yes, life had decided that for him—

332
00:29:29,719 --> 00:29:35,398
—life, and his own infinite curiosity about life. Eternal youth, infinite

333
00:29:35,398 --> 00:29:41,398
passion, pleasures subtle and secret, wild joys and wilder sins— —he was to have all

