00:29:46,680 --> 00:29:51,520
all. A feeling of pain crept over him as he thought of the desecration that was

336
00:29:51,520 --> 00:29:57,760
in store for the fair face on the canvas. Once, in boyish mockery of

337
00:29:57,760 --> 00:30:04,799
Narcissus, he had kissed, or Fain to kiss, those painted lips that now smiled so cruy at

338
00:30:04,799 --> 00:30:09,478
him. Morning after morning he had sat before the portrait wondering at its

339
00:30:09,478 --> 00:30:14,680
beauty, almost enamored of it, as it seemed to him at times. Was it to alter

