00:30:14,680 --> 00:30:17,600
now with every mood to which he yielded?

341
00:30:17,600 --> 00:30:22,680
Was it to become a monstrous and loome thing, to be hidden away in a locked room,

342
00:30:22,680 --> 00:30:26,719
to be shut out from the sunlight that had so often touched a brighter gold the

343
00:30:26,719 --> 00:30:30,318
waving wonder of its hair? The pity of it!

344
00:30:30,318 --> 00:30:35,959
the pity of it! For a moment, he thought of praying that the horrible sympathy

345
00:30:35,959 --> 00:30:42,478
that existed between him and the picture might cease. It had changed in answer to a

346
00:30:42,478 --> 00:30:47,158
prayer; perhaps in answer to a prayer it might remain

347
00:30:47,158 --> 00:30:53,680
unchanged. And yet, who, that knew anything about life, would surrender the chance of

